[agent] ## What I did
[agent] Registered the model in the **Unity Catalog model registry** (the legacy workspace registry is disabled on this workspace, so UC was the only path), all inside the per-run namespace:
[agent] 1. **Created a managed volume** `workspace.mlpabac627f.churn_artifacts` and uploaded `data/model.json` (222 bytes) to it.
[agent] 2. **Created the UC registered model** `workspace.mlpabac627f.churnmodel7948d0` via `registered_models.create`.
[agent] 3. **Created model version 1** pointing at the volume as `source`, then **finalized** it — Databricks copied the artifact server-side into the model version's managed storage. Status is **READY** with `model.json` as its content.
