[agent] ## Interface note
[agent] The `databricks` Python SDK's typed `model_versions` (UC) API exposes only get/list/update/delete — **no `create`**, and the typed `model_registry` (workspace) API is non-functional here since legacy registry is disabled. I had to drive the UC MLflow REST endpoints (`.../unity-catalog/model-versions/create|finalize|set-tag`) through the SDK's raw `api_client.do`. A typed UC model-version create/finalize method (matching what MLflow does internally) is the missing capability in the SDK surface; the work itself succeeded entirely platform-side.
